Conceptual Acknowledgments:
- The pattern of rendering transparent SVG statistics inside scheduled GitHub
  Actions workflows without external servers was inspired by prior open-source
  work in jstrieb/github-stats and rahul-jha98/github-stats-transparent.
  DataProfile is an independent, clean-room implementation written from scratch
  in Go with its own domain model, notebook normalizer, multi-source collectors,
  and visualization grammars.
- The four visualization schools implemented in this engine draw on the
  published works of Edward Tufte (The Visual Display of Quantitative
  Information, 1983), Stephen Few (Information Dashboard Design, 2006),
  Alberto Cairo (The Functional Art, 2012; The Truthful Art, 2016), and
  Nigel Holmes (Designer's Guide to Creating Charts and Diagrams, 1984)
  alongside Otto Neurath's ISOTYPE system.
